                </a>

    


</div>
</div>
</div><div id="purpose" class="bde-fancy-container-2245-106 bde-fancy-container">
  
  
	



<h2 class="bde-heading-2245-121 bde-heading">
AI Is a Tool, Not the Author
</h2><p class="bde-f-text-2245-122 bde-f-text">
NBA Salaries covers every player under contract and all 30 team payrolls. Keeping that accurate through a season of trades, waivers and extensions is a lot of data for one editor, and AI makes it manageable.
</p><p class="bde-f-text-2245-123 bde-f-text">
Claude, made by Anthropic, does most of the work: it reads transaction reports, compares contract figures across sources, drafts the copy on player and team pages, and helps build the page templates. Dan Sweeting sets the rules it works to and decides what is published.
</p>
</div><div id="coverage" class="bde-fancy-container-2245-107 bde-fancy-container">
  
  
	



<h2 class="bde-heading-2245-124 bde-heading">
How a Page Is Built
</h2><div class="bde-fancy-container-2245-125 bde-fancy-container">
  
  
	



<div class="bde-fancy-container-2245-135 bde-fancy-container">
  
  
	



<div class="bde-fancy-container-2245-143 bde-fancy-container">
  
  
	



<div class="bde-f-text-2245-158 bde-f-text">
Research
</div>
</div><h3 class="bde-heading-2245-144 bde-heading">
Every Move, With a Source
</h3><p class="bde-f-text-2245-145 bde-f-text">
AI reads the NBA's transaction log, team announcements, Basketball-Reference, RealGM and Hoops Rumors, and records each signing, trade, waiver and option decision with where it came from.
</p>
</div><div class="bde-fancy-container-2245-136 bde-fancy-container">
  
  
	



<div class="bde-fancy-container-2245-146 bde-fancy-container">
  
  
	



<div class="bde-f-text-2245-159 bde-f-text">
Check
</div>
</div><h3 class="bde-heading-2245-147 bde-heading">
Two Sources, and the Sums
</h3><p class="bde-f-text-2245-148 bde-f-text">
Each change is matched against a second source, and team payrolls are recalculated from the individual contracts. When sources disagree, the change waits until it is settled.
</p>
</div><div class="bde-fancy-container-2245-137 bde-fancy-container">
  
  
	



<div class="bde-fancy-container-2245-149 bde-fancy-container">
  
  
	



<div class="bde-f-text-2245-160 bde-f-text">
Write
</div>
</div><h3 class="bde-heading-2245-150 bde-heading">
Copy From Checked Data
</h3><p class="bde-f-text-2245-151 bde-f-text">
Claude writes the explanations from the checked figures only, so the copy never quotes a number the database doesn't hold.
</p>
</div>
</div>
</div><div id="standards" class="bde-fancy-container-2245-108 bde-fancy-container">
  
  
	



<h2 class="bde-heading-2245-126 bde-heading">
What AI Doesn't Do
</h2><div class="bde-fancy-container-2245-127 bde-fancy-container">
  
  
	



<div class="bde-fancy-container-2245-138 bde-fancy-container">
  
  
	



<h3 class="bde-heading-2245-152 bde-heading">
No AI Images
</h3><p class="bde-f-text-2245-153 bde-f-text">
Every image on the site is a team logo or an official player headshot. Nothing is AI-generated.
</p>
</div><div class="bde-fancy-container-2245-139 bde-fancy-container">
  
  
	



<h3 class="bde-heading-2245-154 bde-heading">
No Invented Figures
</h3><p class="bde-f-text-2245-155 bde-f-text">
If a salary, guarantee or option hasn't been reported, the page says so rather than filling the gap with a guess.
</p>
</div><div class="bde-fancy-container-2245-140 bde-fancy-container">
  
  
	



<h3 class="bde-heading-2245-156 bde-heading">
No AI Bylines
</h3><p class="bde-f-text-2245-157 bde-f-text">
Articles carry the name of the person responsible for them. AI tools are never listed as authors.
</p>
</div>
</div><div class="bde-fancy-container-2245-128 bde-fancy-container">
  
  
	



